<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.Above unaudited results were reviewed by Audit Committee, approved  and  taken on record by the Board at its meeting held on 12.11.21, in terms of Reg. 33 of SEBI (LODR) Reg, 2015. 2.Group is adopting IND AS and the financial results for the quarter and half year ended 30.9.21. 3.Status of production and related activities of Holding Company (HC) remains unchanged during the quarter under review. 4.No Interest has been provided in the books of account of the HC for the quarter ended 30.9.21 on the financial facilities availed from the banks/financial institutions.  HC has however arrived at a settlement with the secured lenders on 9.8.21 for the settlement of all outstanding dues (other than the debt allocated to the Vizag Plant of Rs.47.50 Cr.) for Rs.95 Cr. over a specified period of time in tranches. Expenditure will be suitably dealt with in the books of account of the Holding Company as and when it is paid.  5.Status of HC's Chennai Insulator division and Vizag Insulator division as “Discontinued Operations” and TPB Segment as “Continuing Operations” remains unchanged during quarter under review. Accordingly adjustments are shown separately in the statement of profit and loss under Ind AS 105. 6.Secured lenders of the HC has informed the company of their outstanding amounts as on 30.7.21 at the time of executing settlement agreements arrived with them on 9.8.21.  Outstanding dues claimed by the secured lenders as on 30.7.21 was: (i)Rs.568.04 cr., from Edelweiss Asset Reconstruction Company Limited (in its capacity as Trustee of EARC SAF 1 Trust, EARC Trust SC 168, EARC Trust SC 209), (ii) Rs.124.75 cr., from IDBI Trusteeship Service Ltd (as a debenture trustee on behalf of debenture holders) and (iii)Rs.201.41 cr., from Allium Finance P Ltd. The claim amounts include interest up to the said period and other charges as provided for under the respective financing documents entered into by the HC. 7.As required under Ind AS 36 Impairment amounting to Rs.4597.53 Lakhs  has been provided for the Quarter ended 30.9.21 in the books of Vizag Insulator Division (considered as discontinued) of the HC with reference to  Land on unexpired Lease period (as on 30.9.21),  Buildings on Card Rate and other fixed assets on the respective WDV basis. The provision made in the earlier Quarter ended 30.6.21 amounting to Rs.4596.90 Lakhs stands reversed. 8.HC clarifies that its Project business vertical is currently functioning at a low scale because of inadequacy of funds. However, HC is evaluating various steps in connection with the re-vitalization and long term stability and growth of its TPBU which potential and opportunity exists once the balance sheet is restructured. HC is also in the process of exploring various options for effective usage of  its industrial land in Chennai in compliance with various approvals and regulations based on its previous experience. These steps are intended to set the foundation for the revival of activities of the HC. Hence, HC continues to prepare its Accounts and the Statement of financial results on a ‘going concern’ basis of accounting. 9.Consolidated financial statements relate to W.S. Industries (I) Ltd (the Parent Company), and its Subsidiary Companies. Parent Company with its subsidiaries constitute the Group.10.Subsidiary Companies considered in the consolidated financial statements are Vidagara Tech Park P Ltd and WS Insulators P Ltd, whose country of incorporation are in India and the percentage of voting power by W.S. Industries (I) Ltd as on 30.9.21 is 100% and 100% respectively. 11. Group is not required to provide Segment Reporting under the criteria specified in IND AS 108. 12.There was no restriction on the functioning of HC and its subsidiaries specifically due to Covid-19. 13.Figures have been regrouped/reclassified wherever necessary, to conform to this period's classifications and as per amended schedule iii to Com. Act, 2013 vide Notification dated 24.3.21.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
